.TH SAPHIRA-IMAGE 8 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
saphira-image \- build bootable Saphira disk images from a profile
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira-image build
.B --profile
.I PROFILE
.B --output
.I IMAGE
.RB [ --size
.IR 4G ]
.RB [ --repository
.IR REPO ]
.RB [ --hostname
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ --root-password
.IR PW ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B saphira-image build
creates a bootable disk image for
.IR PROFILE :
a GPT-partitioned raw disk (1 MiB bios-boot for GRUB i386-pc plus a
Linux root partition), formatted ext4, filled by
.BR saphira-install (8)
through the shared assembler, with GRUB installed from inside the
target so core.img and modules always come from the same grub
package. Output ending in
.I .qcow2
is converted with
.BR qemu-img ;
anything else stays raw.
.PP
Layout reserves EFI from day one: a later ESP partition slots beside
bios-boot and root with no re-layout, and
.B --target=i386-pc
gains an
.B x86_64-efi
sibling then. BIOS-only is the first milestone, not the format.
.PP
Requires root privileges (loop devices, mkfs, mounts, GRUB to a
device) and host tools
.BR sfdisk ,
.BR losetup ,
.BR mkfs.ext4
and
.BR grub-install ;
.B qemu-img
is required only for
.I .qcow2
output. Like
.BR installpkg ,
this is a privileged admin boundary: it never belongs in the
rootless package build path.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --profile " " \fIPROFILE
Profile name from
.BR saphira-profiles (5)
(required).
.TP
.BR --output " " \fIIMAGE
Output path (required, must not exist).
.I .qcow2
suffix selects qcow2 conversion.
.TP
.BR --size " " \fI4G
Raw disk size (default
.BR 4G ;
.BR G / M / K
suffixes).
.TP
.BR --repository " " \fIREPO
APK repository, passed through to the install.
.TP
.BR --hostname " " \fINAME
Hostname to write (default: the profile name).
.TP
.BR --root-password " " \fIPW
Root password for automated boot-test images (default: locked,
firstboot owns accounts). Throwaway only; rotate on first real use.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Image ready; loop detached, workspace removed.
.TP
.B 1
Any failure; partial image removed, loop detached. The raw file is
deleted on failure (a half-written disk is never left behind).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Boot-testable virtualisation host, 4 GiB qcow2:
.PP
.RS
sudo saphira-image build --profile virtualisation-host \\
    --output virt-host.qcow2 --repository /out/stage4/packages/hatched \\
    --root-password test
.RE
.PP
 Raw image for dd to a USB stick:
.PP
.RS
sudo saphira-image build --profile virtualisation-host \\
    --output virt-host.raw --size 8G
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira-install (8),
.BR saphira-assemble-rootfs (8),
.BR saphira-profiles (5),
.BR grub-install (8),
.BR qemu-img (1)
